WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.063 --> 00:00:18.913
Morb, troll, and the entire room faded from view as Zann slid into the wormhole behind Wyssa.

2
00:00:19.654 --> 00:00:22.676
It was like nothing he'd ever seen or experienced before.

3
00:00:23.537 --> 00:00:25.618
It felt like falling—or flying.

4
00:00:25.999 --> 00:00:29.321
Zann found it difficult to breathe or think as he plummeted forward.

5
00:00:30.142 --> 00:00:31.183
Or was it downward?

6
00:00:31.523 --> 00:00:32.084
Or upward?

7
00:00:32.864 --> 00:00:36.045
He couldn't tell, and it made him feel dizzy and confused.

8
00:00:36.766 --> 00:00:39.427
He put out his free hand, trying to slow himself down.

9
00:00:40.447 --> 00:00:43.589
But there was nothing to grab, and his body twisted wildly.

10
00:00:43.609 --> 00:00:45.450
"Be careful!"

11
00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:47.430
Wyssa's voice echoed strangely.

12
00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:50.372
"Do not pull yourself off course!"

13
00:00:51.232 --> 00:00:54.213
Zann opened his mouth to answer but no words came out.

14
00:00:54.914 --> 00:00:55.614
He looked around.

15
00:00:56.394 --> 00:00:59.856
The wormhole was dark, filled with swirling shapes and colors.

16
00:01:00.712 --> 00:01:03.814
Every few seconds he and Wyssa slid past bright spots.

17
00:01:04.875 --> 00:01:06.255
Were those other wormholes?

18
00:01:06.976 --> 00:01:08.617
Did some of them lead to different worlds?

19
00:01:09.517 --> 00:01:11.718
Zann tried to focus on the next one they approached.

20
00:01:12.479 --> 00:01:16.761
He stared through it as they passed by, trying to catch a glimpse of what lay beyond.

21
00:01:17.582 --> 00:01:24.786
He saw a peaceful field of tall, amber grasses waving in the breeze with huge, strange-looking animals grazing.

22
00:01:25.546 --> 00:01:31.031
The sky above was a clear, pale purple; a pair of silver suns shone down on the scene.

23
00:01:32.132 --> 00:01:35.935
That was all Zann was able to take in before he was past the wormhole, but it was

24
00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:37.456
enough to set his mind spinning.

25
00:01:38.237 --> 00:01:39.098
It was amazing.

26
00:01:39.458 --> 00:01:41.080
How many different worlds were out there?

27
00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:42.161
What were they like?

28
00:01:42.981 --> 00:01:45.223
No wonder his parents had loved exploring so much!

29
00:01:45.924 --> 00:01:50.829
When the next wormhole appeared, Zann reached out to grab its edge, hoping to slow down so he

30
00:01:50.849 --> 00:01:51.709
could get a good look.

31
00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:54.152
The movement sent him twisting sideways.

32
00:01:55.264 --> 00:01:58.347
This time he felt his hand start to slip from Wyssa's grip.

33
00:01:58.367 --> 00:02:04.192
"No!" Wyssa yelled harshly, grabbing him with both hands and yanking him forward.

34
00:02:04.972 --> 00:02:07.114
Zann glanced back longingly at the wormhole.

35
00:02:07.855 --> 00:02:09.416
He hadn't seen much more this time.

36
00:02:10.197 --> 00:02:14.961
Mostly swirling blue-green water with large, dark shapes drifting through it.

37
00:02:15.782 --> 00:02:18.184
Was it an ocean, perhaps one in Magica?

38
00:02:18.924 --> 00:02:22.648
Or could it be yet another faraway world full of wondrous creatures?

39
00:02:23.712 --> 00:02:27.414
Wyssa pulled him even with her; her eyes flashed angrily in the darkness.

40
00:02:27.434 --> 00:02:29.895
"I told you not to do that!"

41
00:02:30.275 --> 00:02:30.815
she scolded.

42
00:02:30.835 --> 00:02:33.356
"This is no place for amateurs.

43
00:02:34.057 --> 00:02:38.919
Do not try to stop or slow down again unless you wish to stay lost like your parents."

44
00:02:39.879 --> 00:02:41.880
Zann frowned, wanting to protest.

45
00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:45.462
But he was distracted by yet more wormholes flashing by.

46
00:02:46.222 --> 00:02:50.304
How could Wyssa just slide past them, ignoring the incredible scenes within?

47
00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:57.242
Then instead of rushing headlong, they were slowing down, though Zann couldn't tell how Wyssa had made that

48
00:02:57.302 --> 00:03:00.363
happen. They were approaching another bright spot.

49
00:03:01.043 --> 00:03:06.204
Wyssa reached out with her free hand, and before Zann realized what was happening, they were through the

50
00:03:06.244 --> 00:03:10.446
wormhole. "Oof," he grunted, landing facedown on the ground.

51
00:03:11.666 --> 00:03:15.387
Zann's head was reeling, and for a moment all he could do was lie there.

52
00:03:16.807 --> 00:03:22.450
Finally he pushed himself up and saw that they'd emerged beside the ancient tree in Wormwood.

53
00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:26.491
"Wow!" he said, once he'd caught his breath enough to speak.

54
00:03:27.332 --> 00:03:28.592
"That was amazing!

55
00:03:29.192 --> 00:03:31.873
How did you learn how to find wormholes like that?

56
00:03:32.714 --> 00:03:34.374
How did you know which one led here?

57
00:03:35.195 --> 00:03:38.196
How did you—" Wyssa cut him off with a frown.

58
00:03:38.216 --> 00:03:40.817
"You need to get out of town.

59
00:03:41.217 --> 00:03:42.578
Morb will be coming for you."

60
00:03:43.358 --> 00:03:48.080
Reaching into a knothole in the tree, she pulled out a large cloth bag and opened it.

61
00:03:48.812 --> 00:03:52.095
Taking out a small object, she pressed it into Zann's hand.

62
00:03:52.115 --> 00:03:58.499
"If you ever see your grandfather again," she added, a little more softly, "give this to him.

63
00:03:58.859 --> 00:03:59.340
Now go."

64
00:04:00.481 --> 00:04:02.482
Zann looked down to see what she'd given him.

65
00:04:03.183 --> 00:04:05.304
It was a smooth, oblong stone.

66
00:04:06.065 --> 00:04:11.169
Its surface was a blend of swirling colors that seemed to shift and change with every glint of

67
00:04:11.189 --> 00:04:11.609
the sun.

68
00:04:11.629 --> 00:04:13.170
"What is it?"

69
00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:13.931
he asked.

70
00:04:14.711 --> 00:04:15.552
Wyssa didn't answer.

71
00:04:16.316 --> 00:04:21.561
Zann glanced up just in time to see her disappear back into the wormhole, clutching her bag.

72
00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:25.164
A second later the wormhole disappeared too.

73
00:04:25.944 --> 00:04:27.306
"Wait!" Zann cried.

74
00:04:27.966 --> 00:04:31.649
That wormhole was the only way he could ever hope to find his parents.

75
00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:35.653
And the only person who could help him travel through it was gone.

76
00:04:36.433 --> 00:04:38.695
Zann could never go through the wormhole by himself.

77
00:04:39.156 --> 00:04:39.616
Or could he?

78
00:04:39.636 --> 00:04:43.740
"I could probably figure out how it works," he thought.

79
00:04:44.796 --> 00:04:49.160
After all, he'd been waiting for an opportunity like this for four years, and here it was.

80
00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:54.044
All he had to do was step in, and he could be reunited with his mom and dad.

81
00:04:54.804 --> 00:04:55.645
It was now or never.

82
00:04:56.425 --> 00:04:59.108
Zann walked over to the tree, and the wormhole opened up.

83
00:04:59.868 --> 00:05:04.932
He gazed into the whirling darkness, took a deep breath, and put the stone in his pocket.

84
00:05:05.753 --> 00:05:09.516
As he did so, he felt something else in there—the troll talisman.

85
00:05:10.937 --> 00:05:12.919
Zann took the talisman out and looked at it.

86
00:05:14.628 --> 00:05:19.431
Trolls Morb What good would it do to bring his parents back to a world where virtually everyone

87
00:05:19.451 --> 00:05:20.652
was a prisoner of Morb?

88
00:05:21.513 --> 00:05:25.736
Magica needed Zann, and right now that was more important than his own needs.

89
00:05:26.516 --> 00:05:29.098
People were counting on him—he couldn't let them down.

90
00:05:29.838 --> 00:05:32.960
Zann took a step back, and the wormhole disappeared once more.

91
00:05:33.961 --> 00:05:37.103
When Zann turned around, a message moth was fluttering toward him.

92
00:05:37.804 --> 00:05:39.825
He reached out and let it land on his finger.

93
00:05:40.546 --> 00:05:43.908
It was from Fala, telling him where to meet her and the others in the forest.

94
00:05:44.713 --> 00:05:48.261
Zann let the message moth go and put the talisman back in his pocket.

95
00:05:49.002 --> 00:05:52.871
He took one last look at the ancient tree and then set out toward the forest.
